numpy 1.24.4  mpmath 1.4.1  python 3.11.15
#### module functions of the six series kinds
ok   polyval(x, c) = sum c_i B_i(x) from the recurrence in mpmath at x in [-3.0, -1.0, -0.5, 0.0, 0.3, 1.0, 2.5, 10.0]  (max rel err 0.0e+00; c=[-2, 0, 1, -3, -2, -3])
ok   polyval scalar x returns a 0-d result equal to the mpmath value
ok   polyval at a complex point equals the recurrence with complex x
ok   polyval(x, c 2-D, tensor=True): shape c.shape[1:] + x.shape, column k evaluated at every x
ok   polyval(tensor=False): shape c.shape[1:], column k evaluated at x[k]
ok   polyval2d(x, y, c) = sum c_ij B_i(x) B_j(y) exactly (Fraction)
ok   polygrid2d: shape x.shape + y.shape, entry [i, j] = p(x[i], y[j])
ok   polyval3d(x, y, z, c) = sum c_ijk B_i(x) B_j(y) B_k(z) exactly
ok   polygrid3d: shape x.shape + y.shape + z.shape on the Cartesian product
ok   polyvander(x, 5): V[..., i] = B_i(x) (recurrence in mpmath), shape x.shape + (6,)
ok   polyvander2d(x, y, [3, 2]): column (deg[1]+1)*i + j = B_i(x) B_j(y); V @ c.flat = val2d
ok   polyvander3d(x, y, z, [2, 2, 1]): column (d1+1)(d2+1) i + (d2+1) j + k = B_i(x) B_j(y) B_k(z); V @ c.flat = val3d
ok   polyfit(x, y, deg=3) = exact least-squares coefficients in the poly basis (Fraction normal equations)  (max rel err 1.3e-13)
ok   polyfit(full=True): [resid, rank, sv, rcond] with resid = sum of squared residuals, rank 4, 4 singular values, rcond = len(x)*eps  (resid 4.20582 exact 4.20582)
ok   polyfit(deg=[0, 2, 3]): 'only those terms' -- coefficient of degree 1 exactly 0, the rest the exact LS over B_0, B_2, B_3
ok   polyfit(w=): 'weight w[i] applies to the unsquared residual' -> minimises sum (w_i r_i)^2 (normal equations with w^2)
ok   polyfit with 2-D y: one fit per column, coefficients in the columns
ok   polyroots(c) = mpmath.polyroots of the equivalent power series (degree 5, 4 complex)  (max abs err 1.4e-15, |root| <= 1.25)
ok   polyroots: 'if all the roots are real then out is also real' (roots -3/2, -1/3, 1/2, 2)
ok   polycompanion(c): (deg, deg) matrix whose eigenvalues are the roots (vs mpmath)
ok   polyfromroots: product (x - r_i) expanded exactly in the poly basis  (coef [0.75, 1.625, -5.875, -1.25, 1.0])
ok   polyfromroots with complex roots returns a complex array (documented) whose values are the exact real expansion
ok   polyder(c, m=2, scl=3): exact second derivative times scl**2 (documented 'multiplication by scl**m')
ok   polyder(c, 0) returns c unchanged; der beyond the degree gives [0]
ok   polyint(c, m=2, k=[1,-2], lbnd=1/2, scl=3): each step = scl * antiderivative, then constant so the value at lbnd is k[i]  (max rel err 1.5e-16)
ok   polyint(c, k=7/3, lbnd=-1.5): value of the integral at lbnd equals k
ok   polyint: default lbnd=0, k=[] -> value 0 at 0; m=0 leaves c unchanged
ok   polyint raises ValueError for len(k) > m and for scl / lbnd non-scalar
ok   polyadd / sub of different lengths: exact (aligned at the low end)
ok   polymul: exact product expanded in the poly basis (linearisation)
ok   polymulx: multiplication by x exact (uses the recurrence)
ok   polydiv: quotient and remainder exact (deg rem < deg divisor)  (quotient [-1.592593, -1.111111, 0.666667], remainder [3.592593, 1.518519])
ok   polydiv by a higher-degree series: quotient [0], remainder the dividend
ok   polypow(c, 3) exact; pow(c, 0) = [1]; pow > maxpower raises ValueError
ok   polyline(off=2.5, scl=-1.5) represents off + scl*x (exact in the poly basis)
ok   polyline(off, 0) is the constant [off]
ok   poly functions trim trailing zeros of the inputs ('c is a trimmed copy'): add([1,2,0,0],[0,0,0]) -> [1,2]
