ok   poly1d indexing p[k] = coefficient of x^k (documented; p.c[-(k+1)]); p[k > order] = 0
ok   poly1d __setitem__ beyond the order extends the polynomial (p[4] = 5 -> 5x^4 + x^2 + 2x + 3)
ok   poly1d strips leading zero coefficients: poly1d([0,0,1,2]).order == 1, .c == [1,2]; poly1d([0]) is the zero polynomial of order 0
