#### np.polyfit beyond n2
ok   np.polyfit(deg=0, cov=True): coefficient = mean(y); cov = RSS/(n-1) / n (documented chi2/dof scaling, dof = M - (deg+1))  (cov 5103.12 exact 5103.12)
ok   np.polyfit(deg=0, cov='unscaled'): cov = (A^T A)^-1 = 1/n
ok   np.polyfit(cov=True) raises ValueError when the number of points does not exceed the order
   np.polyfit(years 2000-2020, deg=5): RankWarning raised = True; exact LS coefficients (highest first) [-1.4151057360102991e-06, 0.01407109290404485, -55.81712277268207, 110404.90336166951, -108880658.93746123, 42824583697.76848]
   returned coefficients [-4.529353851916963e-08, 0.0003044716609235685, -0.4754357036658827, -831.2937652827712, 2910788.7455400326, -2115070142.3401709]; relative errors per coefficient ['9.7e-01', '9.8e-01', '9.9e-01', '1.0e+00', '1.0e+00', '1.0e+00']; fitted-value error 9.71e-06 relative to max|y| (informational)
   full=True: rank 5 of 6, singular values [2.4494573303959988, 0.01260103006145663, 2.4712301305933383e-05, 2.845388262243942e-08, 2.0716740599515805e-11, 8.835966618956166e-15], rcond 4.663e-15 = len(x)*eps = 4.663e-15
ok   np.polyfit(full=True) returns (coef, residuals, rank, singular_values, rcond) with rcond = len(x)*eps and residuals = sum of squared residuals of ITS fit
ok   np.polyfit issues RankWarning exactly when full=False and rank < order (rank from full=True: 5)
ok   np.polyfit degree 5 on the centred years (x - 2010): coefficients equal the exact LS to 1e-9 relative (the documented remedy)  (max rel err 1.8e-12)
ok   np.polyfit with complex y (real x): coefficients = LS(real y) + i LS(imag y), complex dtype
ok   np.polyfit with int y: float64 output equal to the exact fit (interpolating 1 + x + x^2)
ok   np.polyfit(w=): 'w[i] applies to the unsquared residual' -> minimises sum (w_i (y_i - p(x_i)))^2, i.e. w = 1/sigma, not 1/sigma^2  (max rel err 1.5e-11)
ok   np.polyfit(w=) with a weight vector of the wrong length raises TypeError; deg < 0 ValueError; x 2-D TypeError
ok   np.polyfit with 2-D y: 'coefficients for the k-th data set are in p[:, k]'
ok   numpy.polynomial.polynomial.polyfit returns low -> high, np.polyfit high -> low: reversed arrays
   degree-20 fit of cos(3u), u=(x-2010)/10, 200 points: Chebyshev.fit rank 21 cond 2.86e+00 max resid 3.6e-14; Polynomial.fit rank 21 cond 9.08e+06 max resid 3.8e-14; raw np.polyfit rank 6 cond 6.97e+16 max resid 4.6e-02 (RankWarning True)
ok   Chebyshev.fit at degree 20 on years 2000-2020 is full rank (21) and reproduces the smooth data to 1e-8 ('better conditioned', documented)
ok   Chebyshev.fit degree 20: the Chebyshev coefficients decay (|c_20| < 1e-10 |c_0|) as a smooth function's should (informational threshold)
